# Backend conventions

## Layers

- Flow: `routes` → `controllers` → `services` (target) → Prisma via `lib/prisma`
- Controllers: Zod validation, HTTP status, call service; keep thin
- Services: business rules and Prisma access; no `req`/`res`
- Routes: mount handlers and middlewares only

## Errors & auth

- Throw `AppError` for expected failures; use the shared error middleware
- Auth: JWT from env (`config/auth`); never hardcode secrets
- Never return `password` (or password hash) in JSON responses
- Role checks via authorization middleware, not ad-hoc string checks scattered in controllers when a pattern already exists

## Uploads & static files

- Upload config lives under `config/`; disk helpers under `utils/`
- Protected file access should require authentication (Phase 2 security work)

## Style

- Match existing file naming (`kebab-case` controllers, routes, middlewares)
- Prefer flat folders under `src/` over inventing `modules/`
